    "body": "Allows moving docstrings and function names into the compressed string block and reusing them as unicode strings.\r\n\r\nMaintains a bit of memory redundancy because the wrapper function of special methods still requires the UTF-8 encoded C string, and the docstring must be defined on the original function to correctly inherit it in subtypes.\r\n\r\nOnly applies to normal functions. Excludes extension type methods because they would require moving the whole type definition as well. It could be applied to our heap type declarations by making a part of the module struct conditional on that feature.",
    "closed_at": null,
